(1) There are to be prescribed classes of visas.
（一）有規定的簽證類別。
Note: See also subsection 35A(4), which allows additional classes of permanent and temporary visas to be prescribed as protection visas by regulations made for the purposes of this subsection.
註：另請參閱第 35A(4) 款，該款允許根據為本款目的製定的法規將額外類別的永久和臨時簽證規定為保護簽證。
(2) As well as the prescribed classes, there are the classes provided for by the following provisions:
(2) 除規定類別外，還有下列條款規定的類別：
(a) section 32 (special category visas);
(a) 第 32 條（特殊類別簽證）；
(b) section 33 (special purpose visas);
(b) 第 33 條（特殊目的簽證）；
(c) section 34 (absorbed person visas);
(c) 第 34 條（被吸收者簽證）；
(d) section 35 (ex ‑ citizen visas);
(d) 第35條（前公民簽證）；
(e) subsection 35A(2) (permanent protection visas);
(e) 第 35A(2) 款（永久保護簽證）；
(f) subsection 35A(3) (temporary protection visas);
(f) 第 35A(3) 款（臨時保護簽證）；
(fa) subsection 35A(3A) (safe haven enterprise visas);
(fa) 第 35A(3A) 款（避風港企業簽證）；
(g) section 37 (bridging visas);
(g) 第 37 條（過橋簽證）；
(h) section 37A (temporary safe haven visas);
(h) 第 37A 條（臨時安全港簽證）；
(i) section 38 (criminal justice visas);
(i) 第 38 條（刑事司法簽證）；
(j) section 38A (enforcement visas);
(j) 第 38A 條（執行簽證）；
(k) section 38B (maritime crew visas).
(k) 第 38B 條（海事船員簽證）。
(3) The regulations may prescribe criteria for a visa or visas of a specified class (which, without limiting the generality of this subsection, may be a class provided for by section 32, 35A, 37, 37A or 38B but not by section 33, 34, 35, 38 or 38A).
(3) 條例可以規定特定類別簽證的標準（在不限製本款一般性的情況下，可以是第 32、35A、37、37A 或 38B 條規定的類別，但不是第 33、34、35、38 或 38A 條規定的類別）。
(3A) To avoid doubt, subsection (3) does not require criteria to be prescribed for a visa or visas including, without limitation, visas of the following classes:
(3A) 為避免疑問，第 (3) 款不要求對一個或多個簽證規定標準，包括但不限於以下類別的簽證：
(a) special category visas (see section 32);
(a) 特殊類別簽證（見第32條）；
(b) permanent protection visas (see subsection 35A(2));
(b) 永久保護簽證（請參閱第 35A(2) 款）；
(c) temporary protection visas (see subsection 35A(3));
(c) 臨時保護簽證（見第 35A(3) 款）；
(ca) safe haven enterprise visas (see subsection 35A(3A));
(ca) 避風港企業簽證（請參閱第 35A(3A) 條）；
(d) bridging visas (see section 37);
(d) 過橋簽證（見第 37 條）；
(e) temporary safe haven visas (see section 37A);
(e) 臨時避難簽證（見第 37A 條）；
(f) maritime crew visas (see section 38B).
(f) 海事船員簽證（見第 38B 條）。
Note 1: An application for any of these visas is invalid if criteria relating to both the application and the grant of the visa have not been prescribed (see subsection 46AA(2)).
註 1：如果未規定與申請和授予簽證相關的標準，則任何此類簽證的申請均無效（請參閱第 46AA(2) 款）。
Note 2: If criteria are prescribed by the regulations for any of these visas, the visa cannot be granted unless any criteria prescribed by this Act, as well as any prescribed by regulation, are satisfied (see subsection 46AA(4)).
註 2：如果法規對這些簽證中的任何一個規定了標準，則除非滿足本法規定的任何標準以及法規規定的任何標準，否則不能授予簽證（請參閱第 46AA（4）款）。
(4) The regulations may prescribe whether visas of a class are visas to travel to and enter Australia, or to remain in Australia, or both.
(4) 法規可以規定某類簽證是前往澳洲並進入澳洲的簽證，或是留在澳洲的簽證，或兩者兼具。
(5) A visa is a visa of a particular class if this Act or the regulations specify that it is a visa of that class.
(5) 若本法或條例明確規定該簽證屬於某一類別的簽證，則該簽證屬於該類別的簽證。

(1) The regulations may make provision for, or in relation to, all or any of the following matters:
(1) 本條例可以對下列全部或任何事項作出規定或與之相關：
(a) when nomination training contribution charge is due and payable;
(a) 提名培訓繳款費到期應付時；
(b) the method of paying nomination training contribution charge (including the currency in which the charge must be paid);
(b) 提名培訓繳費的繳交方式（包括繳費的幣種）；
(c) the remission or refund of nomination training contribution charge;
(c) 提名培訓繳費的減免或退還；
(d) the overpayment or underpayment of nomination training contribution charge;
(d) 多付或少付提名培訓繳費；
(e) the payment of a penalty in relation to the underpayment of nomination training contribution charge;
(e) 支付與少繳提名培訓繳費相關的罰款；
(f) the giving of information and keeping of records relating to a person’s liability to pay nomination training contribution charge.
(f) 提供與個人支付提名培訓繳費責任相關的資訊並保存記錄。
(2) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(e), the penalty payable must be a civil penalty not exceeding 60 penalty units.
(2) 就第 (1)(e) 款而言，應繳納的罰款必須是不超過 60 個罰款單位的民事罰款。

(1) Subject to sections 357A and 367E of this Act, the ART Act applies in relation to a review by the ART of reviewable migration decisions and reviewable protection decisions unless this Part expressly provides otherwise.
(1) 根據本法第 357A 和 367E 條，除非本部分另有明確規定，否則 ART 法適用於 ART 對可審查移民決定和可審查保護決定的審查。
(2) The following provisions of the ART Act do not apply in relation to the review by the ART of reviewable migration decisions or reviewable protection decisions:
(2) 《ART 法》的以下規定不適用於 ART 對可審查移民決定或可審查保護決定的審查：
(a) paragraph 21(2)(b) (notice of application to decision ‑ maker);
(a) 第21(2)(b)段（向決策者發出申請通知）；
(b) paragraph 21(2)(c) (notice of application to other persons made a party to the proceedings);
(b) 第 21(2)(c) 段（向成為訴訟當事人的其他人發出的申請通知）；
(c) subsection 21(3) (notice of application and right to apply to become a party);
(c) 第 21(3) 款（申請通知和申請成為當事人的權利）；
(d) section 23 (decision ‑ maker must give Tribunal reasons and documents—general rule);
(d) 第23條（決策者必須向仲裁庭提供理由和文件－一般規則）；
(e) section 24 (decision ‑ maker must give Tribunal additional statement if Tribunal requires—general rule);
(e) 第24條（如果仲裁庭要求，決策者必須向仲裁庭提供補充說明－一般規則）；
(f) section 25 (decision ‑ maker must give Tribunal additional documents within 28 days—general rule);
(f) 第25條（決策者必須在28天內向仲裁庭提供額外文件－一般規則）；
(g) section 27 (decision ‑ maker must give copies of reasons and documents to other parties—general rule);
(g) 第27條（決策者必須向其他各方提供理由和文件的副本－一般規則）；
(h) section 32 (reviewable decision continues to operate unless Tribunal orders otherwise);
(h) 第 32 條（可重複的決定繼續有效，除非仲裁庭另有命令）；
(i) section 85 (tribunal may remit decision to decision ‑ maker for reconsideration);
(i) 第85條（仲裁庭可將決定提交給決策者重新考慮）；
(ia) section 97 (Tribunal must dismiss application if decision is not reviewable decision);
(ia) 第 97 條（如果決定不是可審查的決定，仲裁庭必須駁回申請）；
(ib) section 98 (Tribunal may dismiss application if fee is not paid);
(ib) 第 98 條（如果未繳交費用，仲裁庭可以駁回申請）；
(j) section 103 (if parties reach agreement—review of decisions only);
(j) 第 103 條（如果雙方達成協議－僅對決定進行審查）；
(k) section 107 (when Tribunal’s decision on review comes into operation);
(k) 第 107 條（仲裁庭的複審決定何時生效）；
(l) section 294 (legal or financial assistance), unless the review is of a decision referred to the guidance and appeals panel by the President of the ART under section 122 of the ART Act.
(l) 第 294 條（法律或財務援助），除非審查是根據 ART 法案第 122 條由 ART 主席提交給指導和上訴小組的決定。
Note: Other provisions of this Part turn off or otherwise modify the operation of other provisions of the ART Act.
註：本部分的其他條款關閉或以其他方式修改 ART 法案其他條款的實施。

(1) A decision under a provision of the ART Act mentioned in subsection (2) is an ART Act migration decision , to the extent that the decision is made in relation to any of the following:
(1) 第 (2) 款中提到的 ART 法案規定下的決定是 ART 法案移民決定，只要該決定是與以下任何一項相關的：
(a) a review of a particular reviewable migration decision or a particular reviewable protection decision;
(a) 對特定可審查移民決定或特定可審查保護決定的審查；
(b) a function of the ART in relation to the exercise of its jurisdiction to review reviewable migration decisions or reviewable protection decisions;
(b) ART 行使管轄權以審查可審查的移民決定或可審查的保護決定的職能；
(c) an ART member in the Migration jurisdictional area;
(c) 移民管轄區內的 ART 成員；
(d) an ART member in the Protection jurisdictional area.
(d) 保護管轄範圍內的 ART 成員。
Note: An ART Act migration decision is a migration decision (see paragraph (d) of the definition of migration decision in subsection 5(1)).
註：ART 法案移民決定是移民決定（請參閱第 5(1) 小節中移民決定定義的 (d) 段）。
