(2) Subregulation (1) does not prevent another Subclass 070 (Bridging (Removal Pending)) visa being granted to the non ‑ citizen, before or after the 12 ‑ month period referred to in subregulation (1) ends, with any one or more of those conditions imposed on the visa.
(2) 第 (1) 款并不妨碍在第 (1) 款所述的 12 个月期限结束之前或之后向非公民发放另一项 070 类（过桥（待递解））签证，并对签证施加任何一项或多项条件。
(3) To avoid doubt, if another Subclass 070 (Bridging (Removal Pending)) visa is granted to the non ‑ citizen with any one or more of those conditions imposed on the visa, then the visa is subject to those conditions for a period of 12 months from the day the visa is granted.
(3) 为避免疑义，如果向该非公民授予另一份 070 子类（过桥（待递解））签证，且该非公民的签证上有任何一项或多项上述条件，则该签证自签证授予之日起 12 个月内须遵守这些条件。

For the purposes of paragraph 109(1)(c) of the Act, the following circumstances are prescribed:
就該法第 109 條第(1)款(c)項而言，規定了以下情況：
(a) the correct information;
(a) 正確的資訊；
(b) the content of the genuine document (if any);
(b) 真實文件的內容（如有）；
(c) whether the decision to grant a visa or immigration clear the visa holder was based, wholly or partly, on incorrect information or a bogus document;
(c) 向簽證持有人發放簽證或移民的決定是否全部或部分基於不正確的資訊或偽造的文件；
(d) the circumstances in which the non ‑ compliance occurred;
(d) 不遵守行為發生的情況；
(e) the present circumstances of the visa holder;
(e) 簽證持有人目前的情況；
(f) the subsequent behaviour of the visa holder concerning his or her obligations under Subdivision C of Division 3 of Part 2 of the Act;
(f) 簽證持有人隨後就其根據該法第 2 部分第 3 節 C 分節所承擔的義務採取的行為；
(g) any other instances of non ‑ compliance by the visa holder known to the Minister;
(g) 部長所知的簽證持有人不遵守規定的任何其他情況；
(h) the time that has elapsed since the non ‑ compliance;
(h) 自未遵守規定以來已過的時間；
(j) any breaches of the law since the non ‑ compliance and the seriousness of those breaches;
(j) 自不遵守法律以來發生的任何違法行為以及這些違法行為的嚴重性；
(k) any contribution made by the holder to the community.
(k) 持有者對社區所做的任何貢獻。
Note: Under s. 109 of the Act, the Minister may cancel a visa if there was non ‑ compliance by the holder of a kind set out in Subdivision C of Division 3 of Part 2 of the Act. The Minister is to have regard to the prescribed circumstances in considering whether to cancel the visa.
註：在 s 下。該法第 109 條規定，如果簽證持有者不遵守該法第 2 部分第 3 部分 C 款規定的規定，部長可以取消簽證。部長在考慮是否取消簽證時應考慮規定的情況。

