(1) The Tribunal may, by order, give directions in relation to the procedure to be followed for a proceeding in the Tribunal.
(1) 仲裁庭可以透過命令，就仲裁庭訴訟程序應遵循的程序發出指示。
(2) The order may do any of the following:
(2) 指令可以執行下列任一操作：
(a) require a party to the proceeding to give information or documents to the Tribunal or another party to the proceeding for the purposes of the proceeding;
(a) 要求訴訟一方為訴訟目的向仲裁庭或訴訟另一方提供資訊或文件；
(b) require a party to the proceeding to give a statement of matters or contentions on which the party intends to rely in the proceeding to the Tribunal or another party to the proceeding;
(b) 要求訴訟一方向仲裁庭或訴訟的另一方提供該方打算在訴訟中依賴的事項或爭議的陳述；
(c) limit the issues on which expert evidence may be given;
(c) 限制可提供專家證據的問題；
(d) limit the number of experts to report on an issue;
(d) 限制某一問題提出報告的專家人數；
(e) require parties to the proceeding to appoint a single person to provide expert evidence;
(e) 要求訴訟各方指定一人提供專家證據；
(f) limit the number of persons to be called to give evidence (either generally or on a specified matter);
(f) 限制被傳喚作證的人數（一般情況或針對特定事項）；
(g) limit the number of persons to appear at a dispute resolution process in relation to the proceeding;
(g) 限制出席與訴訟相關的爭議解決程序的人數；
(h) require expert witnesses to give evidence at the same time;
(h) 要求專家證人同時作證；
(i) limit the time for giving evidence or making oral submissions;
(i) 限製作證或口頭陳述的時間；
(j) limit the length of written submissions;
(j) 限製書面提交資料的長度；
(k) limit the ability of a party to the proceeding to give information or documents to the Tribunal and any other party to the proceeding for the purposes of the proceeding within a period before the start of the hearing of the proceeding.
(k) 限制訴訟一方在訴訟聽證開始前的一段時間內為訴訟目的向仲裁庭和訴訟的任何其他當事人提供資訊或文件的能力。
(3) If the proceeding is for review of a decision, the order may require the decision ‑ maker to give the Tribunal or another party to the proceeding a statement setting out the grounds the decision ‑ maker considers support the decision ‑ maker’s position in relation to the review.
(3) 如果訴訟是為了複審決定，命令可以要求決策者向仲裁庭或訴訟的另一方提供一份聲明，闡明決策者認為支持決策者在覆核中的立場的理由。
(4) Subsections (2) and (3) do not limit this section.
(4) 第(2)和(3)款不限製本條。
(5) Section 55 (right to present case) does not prevent the Tribunal making an order under this section.
(5) 第 55 條（陳述案件的權利）並不妨礙仲裁庭依本條作出命令。

